E158   95 01                  STA   1,X   
E15A   60                     RTS      
E15B                             ; "*": the classic shift-right multiply. The multiplier is the NOS cell: it
E15B                             ; leaves from the bottom while the product comes in at the top, through
E15B                             ; A:T0 above it; after 16 rounds the cell holds the low 16 bits, which are
E15B                             ; all that is kept. Dropping TOS (the multiplicand) leaves it on top.
E15B   A0 10        H_MUL:    LDY   #16   ; the round count
E15D   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E15F   85 04                  STA   T0   ; A:T0 = the upper half
E161   56 03                  LSR   3,X   
