E181                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
E181                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
E181                             ; it stops with Z.
E181                             ; b's cell is dropped once D holds |b|; udiv then leaves the remainder just
E181                             ; where that cell was, so stepping X back down makes it the top cell.
E181                          IF   CHECKED   
E181   A9 5A        E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; divide by zero, the stack as it was
E183   4C 6E E6               JMP   error   
E186                          ENDIF      
E186                H_DIV:       
E186                          IF   CHECKED   
E186   B5 00                  LDA   0,X   
E188   15 01                  ORA   1,X   
E18A   F0 F5                  BEQ   e_zero   
